{"content":[{"c":["SMITH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Worker in metals; a blacksmith. The earliest metalworker mentioned in the Bible is Tubal-cain (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.4.22","r":"Gen.4.22","rawR":"Gen.4.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.4.22","value":"Gen.4.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 4:22"},"). The term covers metalworkers of all kinds: copper, bronze, iron, silver, and gold. Silversmiths are mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.17.4","r":"Judg.17.4","rawR":"Judg.17.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.17.4","value":"Judg.17.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Judges 17:4"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.19.24","r":"Acts.19.24","rawR":"Acts.19.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.19.24","value":"Acts.19.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 19:24"},". Ironsmiths were rare or even nonexistent in Israel up to the time of Samuel, and the Israelites had to go to the Philistine smiths to have their iron tools sharpened (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.13.19","r":"1Sam.13.19","rawR":"1Sam.13.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.13.19","value":"1Sam.13.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 13:19"},"). In the days of the kings, Israelite smiths were active and were subsequently taken into captivity by Nebuchadnezzar (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.24.14-16","r":"2Kgs.24.14-16","rawR":"2Kgs.24.14-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.24.14-16","value":"2Kgs.24.14-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 24:14-16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.24.1","r":"Jer.24.1","rawR":"Jer.24.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.24.1","value":"Jer.24.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 24:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.29.2","r":"Jer.29.2","rawR":"Jer.29.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.29.2","value":"Jer.29.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"29:2"},"). Details of the work of the smith are given in several accounts (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.25.4","r":"Pr.25.4","rawR":"Pr.25.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.25.4","value":"Pr.25.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 25:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.44.12","r":"Isa.44.12","rawR":"Isa.44.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.44.12","value":"Isa.44.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 44:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.54.16","r":"Isa.54.16","rawR":"Isa.54.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.54.16","value":"Isa.54.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"54:16"},"). The smiths mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=Zech.1.20","r":"Zech.1.20","rawR":"Zech.1.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.1.20","value":"Zech.1.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zechariah 1:20"}," are probably ironsmiths or blacksmiths."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MineralsandMetals_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MineralsandMetals_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MineralsandMetals_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Minerals and Metals"},"; ",{"href":"?item=StonesPrecious_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"StonesPrecious_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"StonesPrecious_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Stones, Precious"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Smith","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 4:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.4.22","rawQueryValue":"Gen.4.22","sourceRefExact":"Gen.4.22"},{"anchorText":"Judges 17:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.17.4","rawQueryValue":"Judg.17.4","sourceRefExact":"Judg.17.4"},{"anchorText":"Acts 19:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.19.24","rawQueryValue":"Acts.19.24","sourceRefExact":"Acts.19.24"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 13:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.13.19","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.13.19","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.13.19"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 24:14-16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.24.14-16","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.24.14-16","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.24.14-16"},{"ancho